Implementing Security in Jenkins Pipelines
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Configure Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) in Jenkins using the Role-based Authorization Strategy plugin
Create and manage user accounts with different permission levels
Set up secure user access for different Jenkins jobs and projects
Implement security best practices for Jenkins pipeline management
Understand the principle of least privilege in CI/CD environments
Configure project-based security to restrict access to specific jobs
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with Jenkins fundamentals and pipeline concepts
Knowledge of user management concepts in Linux systems
Understanding of basic security principles and access control concepts
Experience with web-based administration interfaces
